,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954553525,"data":"4. shape sweep: launches should not move with slabs; arithmetic should\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954558214,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954561612,"data":"  If the schedule is a function of the graph and not of the batch size, then\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954565043,"data":"  `launches` is flat in slabs and only the per-slab arithmetic grows. Fitting\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954568448,"data":"  gpu_us(slabs) = fixed + slope*slabs therefore separates the two axes WITHOUT\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954571913,"data":"  converting an instruction count into time by any constant.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.95457527,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954578373,"data":"  reps per candidate in this section: {'A': 1, 'B': 3, 'C': 3, 'D2': 3}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954581752,"data":"  (A is 5,380 launches and seconds of CPU SCHEDULING per realize; repeating it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.95458857,"data":"  over five slab counts would spend the session on it. The cheap candidates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954592009,"data":"  get repeated measurements because they sit near the instrument's floor.)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954595433,"data":"\n"}
