,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954750264,"data":"D2     5       1,181           20.3   0.9666          48.6%      0.01  floor 49% / arith 51%\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954753766,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954756877,"data":"  `fixed` is the launch-dominated floor and `slope` the marginal per-slab\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954760318,"data":"  cost. `ns/MAC` is nanoseconds of device time per algorithmic multiply-add.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954763704,"data":"  If that number is roughly the same for two candidates, device time tracks\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954767148,"data":"  the ALGORITHM's arithmetic. If it differs by an order of magnitude between\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954770595,"data":"  them, device time is tracking the SCHEDULE and the arithmetic column is not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954774011,"data":"  what the card is spending its time on.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954777308,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954780422,"data":"  `launch_counts` per candidate, across the sweep, are in ut_time.json.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954783831,"data":"  If they are not flat in slabs, the fit above does not separate the two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954787183,"data":"  axes the way this section claims, and the note must say so.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954790779,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954793938,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954797439,"data":"5. launch calibration: what does one launch cost on this card?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954805719,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954808695,"data":"  A chain of n dependent one-op kernels, timed with the SAME instrument as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954822493,"data":"  the candidates (DEBUG=2, per-kernel CUDA events). The slope of gpu_us\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954826559,"data":"  against the number of kernels that ACTUALLY LAUNCHED is microseconds per\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954830611,"data":"  launch. This is the number that lets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954834611,"data":"      arithmetic_us = gpu_us - launches * per_launch_us\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954857298,"data":"  be a residual in MICROSECONDS rather than an instruction count times a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954864302,"data":"  constant -- which is what the brief asks for, since the census is not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954867836,"data":"  additive and converting it by a factor would be the error.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954871172,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954874364,"data":"     shape      n  launched      gpu_us  us/launch\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954877696,"data":"--------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954880987,"data":"  1 thread     16        16         311     19.426\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.95488429,"data":"  1 thread     64        64         826     12.902\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954887988,"data":"  1 thread    256       256       2,903     11.341\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954891245,"data":"  1 thread   1024     1,024      11,164     10.902\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954894462,"data":"  1 thread   4096     4,096      43,948     10.729\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954897754,"data":"  1 thread    fit                           10.693   intercept 162 us, R2 1.0000\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954901201,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954904415,"data":"     16 KB     16        16         314     19.650\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954908338,"data":"     16 KB     64        64         836     13.060\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954912163,"data":"     16 KB    256       256       2,993     11.690\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954916319,"data":"     16 KB   1024     1,024      11,796     11.519\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954920735,"data":"     16 KB   4096     4,096      45,157     11.025\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954924856,"data":"     16 KB    fit                           10.986   intercept 231 us, R2 0.9999\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954928266,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954931434,"data":"  MEASURED, DEBUG=2, so these slopes INCLUDE the host launch latency the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954934884,"data":"  instrument charges to every kernel -- which is exactly what the candidate\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954938304,"data":"  measurements are charged too, so the residual below compares like with like.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954941742,"data":"  The `16 KB` row is a sensitivity check: it is what a candidate kernel of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954945156,"data":"  this operator's size costs if it did NOTHING but copy one buffer. The\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954948551,"data":"  headline uses the `1 thread` row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954951823,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954954968,"data":"== residual: gpu_us - launches * per_launch_us   (bench shape) ==\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954958383,"data":"cand  launches      gpu_us   launch_us launch_us@16KB    resid_us   resid %   ns/algMAC  reading\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.95496186,"data":"------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954965295,"data":"A        5,380      94,842      57,528         59,107      37,314     39.3%        1.49  launch-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954968746,"data":"B           86       3,258         920            945       2,338     71.8%        0.09  arithmetic-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954975974,"data":"C           44       2,231         470            483       1,760     78.9%        0.42  arithmetic-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954981234,"data":"D2          41       2,426         438            450       1,987     81.9%        0.02  arithmetic-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.954989665,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955013074,"data":"  ns/algMAC is nanoseconds of NON-LAUNCH device time per algorithmic\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955017159,"data":"  multiply-add, using the algorithm's own MAC count (ut_price.macs) and not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955021252,"data":"  any census figure. Candidates whose entries agree are being priced by the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955025039,"data":"  same axis; candidates whose entries differ by an order of magnitude are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955028406,"data":"  not, and THAT is the finding, not the winner.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955031633,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955035724,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955039216,"data":"7. is the ordering spelling-invariant?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955042431,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955045855,"data":"  notes/31 §2: the `numpy` spelling of a constant costs a COPY kernel each and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955049363,"data":"  the `arange` spelling costs ALU inside every consumer. notes/31 measured the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955052744,"data":"  KERNEL ranking to be identical under both. The TIMING ranking is checked here,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955056153,"data":"  for the two candidates the open question is actually about.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1234.955059442,"data":"\n"}
